<!--T:1-->
Two kinds of wiki pages make a good fit for a feed.

<!--T:2-->
== A blog ==
Some wikis run a blog out of a category, with each post as a page in it. A new page in that category becomes a new Fediverse post. This is the [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Feed kinds#category</tvar>|<code>category</code>]] kind.

<!--T:3-->
== Release notes ==
Some wikis keep a release notes page and add a section to it with each update. A new section becomes a new Fediverse post. This is the [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Feed kinds#section</tvar>|<code>section</code>]] kind.

<!--T:4-->
These sections are often written by a bot, so a feed of this kind counts bot edits.
</translate>

